2. THE 19 SUBCELL ERRORS -- INVESTIGATED, NOT REAL
------------------------------------------------------------------------
`drc listall count` (the per-cell hierarchical count) reports 19 errors that
`drc listall why` does not see in the expanded top cell:

    via_stack_2e2571cb      x3      via_stack_2e2571cb$1    x3
    via_stack_2e2571cb$2    x3      via_stack_2e2571cb$3    x3
    via_stack_918d05dd$2    x3      via_stack_918d05dd$3    x3
    via_stack_686e5d96$33   x1                      TOTAL  19

layout-agent reported these and asked me to decide whether they are real in
context. They are NOT, and I did not take that on trust -- I flattened and
re-checked:

    flatten -dobox -nolabels routed_flat ; load routed_flat ; drc check
    SRC_BBOX  = 26373 14883 105500 94056  (internal units)
    FLAT_BBOX = 26373 14883 105500 94056  -- equal and non-empty, so this is
                not environment.md's "empty-cell false pass"
    FLAT_DRC_TOTAL = 0
    FLATCELLCOUNT lines = 0     <-- all 19 disappear once flattened

Diagnosis: classic out-of-context subcell errors. A via_stack cell drawn alone
is missing the parent's enclosing metal; assembled, the parent completes it.
Class = none (not a violation). Evidence: layout_fixer_work/drc_flat/flat.log.

