5. SPECIFIC RISKS FLAGGED BY layout-agent -- RESOLVED
------------------------------------------------------------------------
* met5.2 coil-to-coil spacing (1.6 um rule vs the placer's global 0.14 um
  min_metal_spacing_um). NOT PRESENT in this seed. layout-agent forced a
  1.6065 um coil gap and that holds. Had it fired it would have been
  class=placement (the placer's clearance model, not the router).
  This remains a latent generator bug: the placer still uses one global
  min_metal_spacing_um and does not know met5's 1.6 um rule, so another seed
  can reproduce it. Reported to the orchestrator, not fixed here (it is a
  placer source fix, out of my scope).
* "DIRTY landing" predictions (voutp on XC0, VDD on XC1): these are
  connectivity predictions, not DRC. Settled in lvs_report.log -- one was a
  false alarm, and see that report for the real story.

