  injected a cell with a 0.05 um met1 gap and a 0.05 um met1 sliver, ran the
  SAME run_drc.py harness -> reported "Metal1 spacing < 0.14um (met1.2)" x2
  with coordinates. The harness reports real violations, so the 0 above is a
  real 0. (It did NOT flag the 0.05 um-wide sliver as a width error, which is
  worth knowing: this harness is demonstrated sensitive to spacing, only
  assumed sensitive to width.)
Plus the bbox guard in section 2, which rules out all three empty-cell false
passes documented in .claude/reference/environment.md.

